//! task: write
//! ask: Same reduction over twenty f32 values, but as a fixed-width pairwise tree of width 8.
//! expect: ok
//! refs: §5.4
//! explain: `forma arborea 8` declares the tree shape as part of the operation: groups of 8 in index order, the last group holding the remainder (20 elements are `[0..8) [8..16) [16..20)`), pairwise inside a group, folded left to right across groups. Floating-point addition is not associative, so the shape is semantics, not an optimization. `+` is one of the associative operators `contrahe` accepts.

publica functio summa_viginti(v: acies<f32, 20>) -> f32 {
    quisque i in 0..20
        contrahe s: +
        forma arborea 8
    {
        s = v[i];
    }
    redde s;
}
